.TH WEATHER 1 "June 2026" "weather CLI" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
weather \- simple CLI tool for weather information (Open-Meteo)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weather
[\fB--city\fR <name>]
[\fB--forecast\fR]
[\fB--days\fR <1-7>]
[\fB--f\fR]
[\fB--c\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
The weather command displays current weather conditions or a multi-day forecast.
It automatically detects your region and switches between Celsius/Fahrenheit and m/s/mph.
Weather data is provided by the Open-Meteo API and requires no API keys.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --city <name>
Show weather for a specific city instead of using IP-based geolocation.

.TP
.B --forecast
Display a weather forecast instead of current conditions.

.TP
.B --days <1-7>
Number of forecast days to display (default: 3).

.TP
.B --f
Force Fahrenheit temperature and mph wind speed.

.TP
.B --c
Force Celsius temperature and m/s wind speed.

.SH AUTOMATIC UNITS
If no unit flags are provided, the tool automatically selects units based on region:
.TP
US, Liberia, Myanmar → Fahrenheit + mph
.TP
Rest of world → Celsius + m/s

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Current weather (auto-detected location):
.B weather

.TP
Weather for a city:
.B weather --city "London"

.TP
3-day forecast:
.B weather --forecast

.TP
7-day forecast:
.B weather --forecast --days 7

.TP
Force Fahrenheit:
.B weather --f

.TP
Force Celsius:
.B weather --c

